{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AppliedDeuteronRealSDP","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AppliedDeuteronRealSDP","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AppliedDeuteronUniqueness"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_realSDP_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_realSDP_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**²H real-SDP optimum is a Subsingleton** among objective-optimal\nfeasible matrices — the uniqueness statement in `Subsingleton`\nform, matching `deuteron_uniqueness_via_empty_sdp` but for the real\nSDP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_realSDP_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_realSDP_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L78-L92","doc":"**²H real-SDP uniqueness, conditional on the solve certificate.**\n\nGiven the real deuteron SDP certificate, the primal optimum is the\nunique feasible matrix achieving the optimal objective.  Fully\nverified by Lean modulo the single `RealSDPCertificate` instance\n(which the numeric dual supplies) — the §3b-cond rigorous-\nconditional pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The dual slack is PosDef (the solve's certificate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.rs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.rs","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The certified real strong-duality pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.sdp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.sdp","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The real per-nucleus SDP at block dimension `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RealSDPCertificate","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L52-L76","doc":"**Real deuteron SDP certificate** (§3b-cond conditional class).\n\nBundles the data the numeric solve\n(`deuteron_real_sdp.py` → `deuteron-real-sdp.witness.json`) produces\nthat Lean cannot yet recompute internally:\n\n* `sdp`     — the real per-nucleus SDP (non-identity cost from the\n              mass formula, branching constraints), at the block\n              dimension `m`.\n* `rs`      — a real strong-duality pair (primal optimum `Φ⋆`, dual\n              `y⋆`) certified by the clarabel/cvxpy solve.\n* `dualSlack_posDef` — the dual slack `S(y⋆) = T − Σ yᵢ⋆ Aᵢ` is\n              positive-definite (strong-duality / strict-\n              complementarity certificate; the bounded positive-norm\n              subspace solve in #1582 supplies this).\n\nA term of this class is exactly the witness's strong-duality\ncertificate.  Everything downstream is proved from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteronBlockCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteronBlockCount","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AppliedDeuteronRealSDP.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Number of Wedderburn blocks for ²H at `H_6` — the partitions\n`λ ⊢ 6`.  `heckeDim 6` is the full algebra dimension; the real SDP\nis block-diagonal, so the *effective* variable count is the number\nof central idempotents `p(6) = 11`.  We work at the block level. ","signatureChunk":0}]}